Note = {2nd International Conference on Education and Education Research (EER
   2015), Paris, FRANCE, MAY 20-21, 2015},
Abstract = {Objective: Analyze the effect of the application of the communication
   skills in the nursing care of the senile patients. Methods: Randomly
   select 148 elderly patients in our hospital, and divide them into two
   groups of the observation group and the control group according to
   whether the communication skills are applied. In the observation group
   of the 74 patients, in the nursing measures, adopt the communication
   skills, while the 74 cases of the patients in the control group are
   given the routine nursing care without the communication skills. Compare
   the nursing effect of the two groups of patients. Results: The SAS
   scores and the SDS scores of the two groups of patients after the
   nursing care decrease significantly than that before the nursing. The
   SAS scores and the SDS scores in the observation group are lower than
   those in the control group after the nursing, P<0.05. The compliance
   rate of the observation group is 88.9\%, while the compliance rate of
   the control group is 75.7\%. Compare the two groups, P<0.05. Conclusion:
   The application of the communication skills in the care for the elderly
   patients can significantly improve the compliance of the patients, and
   relieve the anxiety and depression of the patients, which has high value
   in the clinical application.
   The elderly patients are the special groups at hospitals, and the
   majority of the elderly patients have the low level of education, with
   the poor psychological endurance. During the hospital admission, their
   physical functions are poor, and the immune functions will decrease,
   which will cause the significant increase of the difficulty of the
   treatment of the elderly patients En. With the intensification of the
   aging process of the population, the number of the elderly patients in
   hospitals is significantly increased, and the workload of the nursing
   and treatment of the patients is greatly improved. Usually during the
   treatment and nursing of the elderly patients, the elderly patients have
   different degrees of the physical and mental diseases, and their
   self-care ability is poor, prone to have the loss and loneliness and
   other negative emotions ({[}2-3]). And the difficulty of the
   communication between the nurses and the elderly patients increased
   significantly, and the traditional and single mode of communication is
   difficult to meet the requirements of the current nursing, also cannot
   adapt to the nursing mode the continuous development. The author takes
   the 74 cases of the elderly patients as the example, and takes the
   communication skills in nursing work, and the effect of the application
   is analyzed as follows.},
