Abstract = {Developing the best professional talent is critical to the success of
   planning. Graduate school admissions procedures often rely heavily on
   prior grade point averages and standardized test scores to determine who
   is allowed to study toward planning degrees. The efficacy of these
   credentials in predicting graduate school performance is examined.
