   policy, which is the marginal external cost caused by the increase of
   carbon dioxide emissions. Calculating the social cost of carbon is to
   measure the externality of the carbon, which has a great significance
   for climate policy formulation. We bring the accumulated knowledge in
   climate research to the field of analytical economics. Different from
