   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {The use of antifreeze based on urea or ammonia compounds have result in
   the increasing indoor air pollution owing to emission of ammonia from
   indoor concrete wall. In order to control indoor ammonia, aqueous
   dispersion of nano-TiO2 was prepared and coated on cotton fabric using
   pad-dry-cure process. Then TiO2-coated cotton fabrics was characterized
   by XRD and SEM. The decomposition of ammonia by UV/TiO2 process with
   TiO2-coated cotton fabric was studied under various experimental
   conditions. A design equation of surface catalytic kinetics was
   developed for describing the decomposition of ammonia in air stream. The
   results indicated that increasing dosage of aqueous nano-TiO2 dispersion
   improved the ammonia decomposition. Ammonia was effectively removed by
   decreasing initial ammonia concentration. When relatively humidity level
   was increased to 45\%, the decomposition of ammonia was remarkably
   enhanced, and could be inhibited by excessive moisture.},
