   Tongji Univ, Coll Env Sci \& Engn; Sci Res Publishing},
Abstract = {The usual coal activated carbon was modified by AlCl3 and was used to
   remove the fluorine in the drinking water. The factors of influencing
   the fluorine removal rate, including the AlCl3 concentration, the types
   of the activated carbon, the mass of the sorbent and the adsorption
   time, was studied in the research. The fluorine removal percentage was
   96\% by 8 g/L modified activated carbon in the 10 mg/L fluorine solution
   at 25 degrees C. The results suggest that is an ideal candidate for the
   treatment of fluorine contaminated drinking water.},
