Note = {Annual International Conference on Social and Behavioural Sciences
   (ICSBS), Singapore, SINGAPORE, AUG 14-16, 2017},
Abstract = {The objective of this study is to ensure adequate and all-encompassing
   comprehensive planning approach in order to acquire relevant information
   database ahead the adoption of privatisation policy on electricity in
   Nigeria for better performance. Considering strategic planning approach
   ahead privatisation of electricity service delivery was based on the
   contents analysis of the relevant literatures reviewed and the
   examination of the tenets of various extant approaches that are related
   to public utility planning. The SWOT' and `STEEPLE/PESTLE' strategic
   planning analytical tools' prospect to ensure availability of adequate
   information database ahead of electricity service delivery privatisation
   for better performance. This proposed approach adequacy among other
   approaches considered is an all-encompassing planning approach, with
   theoretical principles and relevant attributes capable of acquiring
   relevant information database, firstly, intending investors need in
   house evaluation and functional condition of electricity facilities on
   ground using SWOT and STEEPLE analytical tools respectively. Several
   literatures reviewed do not consider strategic planning as solution to
   lack of adequate information database about functional condition of
   electricity facilities and the worth of the intending investors were the
   bane of effective electricity service delivery privatisation. Strategic
   planning became imperative as a precautionary approach to public
   utilities privatisation. This proposed approach provides adequate
   economic and physical information database needed ahead the adoption of
   electricity service delivery privatisation.},
