   Sci \& Technol},
Abstract = {Solid-state anaerobic digestion of dewatered sludge was investigated
   under mesophilic conditions and a steady state model was developed to
   help reactor design for solid state anaerobic digestion system of
   dewatered sludge. Biogas yield, volatile solid reduction and methane
   content showed good linear relationship with OLR (or 1/SRT) at long SRTs
   (>= 10d). The minimum SRT at which system failure occurred was 3 days.
   Maximum VS reduction and biogas yield was estimated 44.83\% and 0.420
   l.g(-1) VS(added)(-1)d(-1). First order constant k was 0.24 d(-1). The
   model can be used to predict system performance and help reactor design.
