Organization = {WSEAS},
Abstract = {``PRO-EFFICIENT COLD \& LIGHTING PRODUCTS - PROEFFICIENCY{''} is an
   Intelligent Energy - Europe project coordinated by ESCAN SA Spain. The
   project partners are ESV - Austria, GERTEC - Germany, ISPE - Romania,
   KAPE - Poland, and SWEA - UK
   PROEFFICIENCY project aims to promote pilot promoters' initiatives and
   pilot consumers' projects/actions for the most eco-energy efficient
   products. The pilot promoters' initiatives are carried out in the six
   partners' countries with different target groups and with the same
   objectives promote pro-efficient cold and lighting products for
   residential and tertiary sectors.
   The project is focused on the implementation of pilot initiatives with
   product promoters and groups of product consumers and will monitor the
   effectiveness of the initiatives and actions developed during the
   project.
   Specific objectives of the project are the followings:
   to stimulate the promotion of the most energy-efficient products amongst
   producers and retailers of cold and lighting goods through voluntary,
   initiatives;
   to accelerate market transformation towards more energy-efficient
   products, through the implementation of pilot consumer action plans;
   to monitor the effectiveness of the development initiatives/actions:
   to give special visibility to successful initiatives/actions, to
   motivate organizations to be in the forefront of the market.
   PROEFFICIENCY Project incorporates an important promotion prograinine
   oriented to ``pilot promoters' initiatives and ``pilot consumers'
   projects/actions ``(incorporating European/Local/Regional actors
   (Manufactures, Importers, Retailers, Energy Agencies, Municipalities,
   Residents Associations. others). With such activities, the Project
   intends to contribute in the medium and long term with the EU energy
   objectives: decreasing the energy\_consumption and energy supply
   dependence.
   This project was presented at the Regional Energy Forum FOREN 2008 -
   Neptun, Romania and it won the third prize at the Energy policy and
   generation section.},
