Abstract = {The phenol ratio of separation culture medium was based on the
   components of original wastewater. One efficient
   hydroxybenzene-degrading bacteria Klebsiella pneumoniae strain AU45 was
   seperated from coal chemical industry wastewater. The growth and laccase
   activity of Klebsiella pneumoniae strain AU45 were measured in different
   conditions. The optimum growing conditions: hydroxybenzene 600-1000mg/L,
   temperature 30-40 degrees C, PH 6.5-8; the optimum production conditions
   of laccase: hydroxybenzene 1000mg/L, temperature 35-40 degrees C, PH
   7-7.5. The changes of laccase in 24h was measured in the optimum
   production conditions of laccase. The growth and laccase activity were
   both resisted in the first 0-8h, and increased after 8-12h recovering.
   The results show that this strain have strong recovering ability,
   growing rate, degradation rate and laccse acticvity. (C) 2011 Published
