Abstract = {The characteristics of two major bacterial populations, phosphate
   accumulating organisms and `'G bacterium'', in the anaerobic-aerobic
   biological phosphate removal process are discussed with an emphasis on
   their metabolic functions. It is theoretically indicated that the system
   of the oxidation-reduction balance in the cell enables the anaerobic
   uptake of organic substrates and that this system is essential for the
   microorganisms to survive in anaerobic-aerobic processes.},
