   Work, Moscow, RUSSIA, JUL 16-18, 2007},
Organization = {NATO Sci Peace \& Secur Comm},
Abstract = {This paper provides a comparison of the results obtained by the FLADIS
   field experiments and the results of CFD modeling by Fluent 6.2. FLADIS
   experiments were carried out by the Riso National Laboratory (Rediphem
   database). Experimental trials were done with pressure liquefied
   ammonia. Meteorological conditions and source strength were deten-nined
   from experimental data and simulated using the CFD approach. The initial
   two-phase flow of tile released ammonia was also included. The liquid
   phase was modeled as droplets using discrete particle modeling, i.e.,
   Euler-Lagrangian approach for continuous and discrete phases. Tile
   second part of this task was devoted to the inclusion of obstacles. High
   obstacles which cannot be modeled with increasing surface roughness were
   included. From the results is obvious that such obstacles influence the
   gas dispersion radically.},
